From a3b3631e15280a7605801c4b1c60d09b3e72f453 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 11:04:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/41] firmware: qcom: scm: answer a listener before
 abandoning it

Giving up on a listener that will not settle left the application parked in TZ
waiting for an answer that was never coming, and per this file's own reasoning
that makes every later QSEECOM call return -EBUSY until the device is power
cycled. The id is in hand at that point, so answer failure and let the
application error out instead.

The unexpected-response-type path cannot do the same, because it fires
precisely when the response does not carry a listener id -- there is nothing to
answer. Say in the message that the interface is stuck, rather than leaving the
next person to work out why it went dead.

While here, hoist the id validation above the round check so both paths have it,
and fix the indentation of the line that introduced it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Assisted-by: Kimi:kimi-k3
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 5ecc1f088..c30cdd639 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2179,23 +2179,41 @@ static int qcom_scm_qseecom_service_listeners(struct qcom_scm_qseecom_resp *res)
 
 	while (res->result == QSEECOM_RESULT_INCOMPLETE) {
 		if (res->resp_type != QSEECOM_SCM_RES_QSEOS_LISTENER_ID) {
+			/*
+			 * No listener id to answer with, so the application
+			 * stays parked in TZ and every later QSEECOM call
+			 * returns -EBUSY until the device is power cycled.
+			 * Nothing here can recover it; say so plainly rather
+			 * than leaving the next person to work out why the
+			 * interface went dead.
+			 */
 			dev_err(__scm->dev,
-				"qseecom: incomplete call with unexpected response type %llx\n",
+				"qseecom: incomplete call with unexpected response type %llx; the interface is now stuck until reboot\n",
 				res->resp_type);
 			return -EPROTO;
 		}
 
+		if (res->data > U32_MAX)
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		id = res->data;
+
 		if (++rounds > QSEECOM_MAX_LISTENER_ROUNDS) {
+			/*
+			 * Answer failure before giving up. The application is
+			 * parked in TZ waiting for this listener, and leaving
+			 * it there makes every later QSEECOM call return
+			 * -EBUSY until the device is power cycled -- so tell
+			 * it the request failed and let it error out instead.
+			 */
 			dev_err(__scm->dev,
-				"qseecom: listener %llu will not settle, giving up\n",
-				res->data);
+				"qseecom: listener %u will not settle, failing it\n",
+				id);
+			qcom_scm_qseecom_listener_respond(id,
+					QSEECOM_LISTENER_FAILURE, res);
 			return -ELOOP;
 		}
 
-		if (res->data > U32_MAX)
-		return -EINVAL;
-
-	id = res->data;
 		listener = qcom_scm_qseecom_listener_find(id);
 		if (listener) {
 			status = listener->service(listener);
